#: src/languages/vue.md:12
msgid "Specifying location of TypeScript SDK"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:14
msgid ""
"By default, this extension assumes that you are working in a project with a "
"`node_modules` directory, and searches for the TypeScript SDK inside that "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:17
msgid ""
"This may not always be true; for example, when working in a project that "
"uses Yarn PnP, there is no `node_modules`. For editor support, the "
"[documented](https://yarnpkg.com/getting-started/editor-sdks) approach is to "
"run something like `yarn dlx @yarnpkg/sdks`. In that case, you can provide "
"the following initialization options in your Zed settings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:23 src/languages/vue.md:41 src/languages/vue.md:68
msgid "\"lsp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:24 src/languages/vue.md:42 src/languages/vue.md:72
msgid "\"vue\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:25
msgid "\"initialization_options\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:26
msgid "\"typescript\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:27
msgid "\"tsdk\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:27
msgid "\".yarn/sdks/typescript/lib\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:35
msgid "Settings Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:37
msgid ""
"`lsp.vue.settings` is passed through to the Vue language server (Volar / "
"[`vuejs/language-tools`](https://github.com/vuejs/language-tools)). The "
"following settings are enabled by default:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:43 src/languages/vue.md:70
msgid "\"settings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:44
msgid ""
"// Display inlay hints for the `$event` parameter in inline event handlers.\n"
"        \"vue.inlayHints.inlineHandlerLeading\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:46
msgid ""
"// Display hints when required component props are missing in templates.\n"
"        \"vue.inlayHints.missingProps\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:48
msgid ""
"// Display inlay hints for patterns that wrap component options.\n"
"        \"vue.inlayHints.optionsWrapper\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:50
msgid ""
"// Display inlay hints related to `v-bind` shorthand (`:`).\n"
"        \"vue.inlayHints.vBindShorthand\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:58
msgid ""
"You can find the upstream settings configuration schema [`here`](https://"
"github.com/vuejs/language-tools/blob/"
"ee5041d27940cf6f9a5150635d3b13140a9dff54/extensions/vscode/package."
"json#L252)."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:60
msgid "Note: Some settings (e.g. `vue.editor.focusMode`) may not take effect."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:62
msgid "Using the Tailwind CSS Language Server with Vue"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:64
msgid ""
"To get all the features (autocomplete, linting, etc.) from the [Tailwind CSS "
"language server](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss-intellisense/"
"tree/HEAD/packages/tailwindcss-language-server#readme) in Vue files, you "
"need to configure the language server so that it knows about where to look "
"for CSS classes by adding the following to your `settings.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:69
msgid "\"tailwindcss-language-server\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:71
msgid "\"includeLanguages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:72
msgid "\"html\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:74
msgid "\"experimental\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:75
msgid "\"classRegex\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:76
msgid "\"class=\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:77
msgid "\"class='([^']*)'\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:78
msgid "\":class=\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:79
msgid "\":class='([^']*)'\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:88
msgid ""
"With these settings, you will get completions for Tailwind CSS classes in "
"Vue template files. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/vue.md:90
msgid ""
"```vue\n"
"<template>\n"
"  <!-- Static class attribute -->\n"
"  <div class=\"flex items-center <completion here>\">\n"
"    <p class=\"text-lg font-bold <completion here>\">Hello World</p>\n"
"  </div>\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- Dynamic class binding -->\n"
"  <div\n"
"    :class=\"\n"
"      active ? 'bg-blue-500 <completion here>' : 'bg-gray-200 <completion "
"here>'\n"
"    \"\n"
"  >\n"
"    Content\n"
"  </div>\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- Array syntax -->\n"
"  <div :class=\"['flex', 'items-center', '<completion here>']\">Content</"
"div>\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- Object syntax -->\n"
"  <div\n"
"    :class=\"{\n"
"      'flex <completion here>': isFlex,\n"
"      'block <completion here>': isBlock,\n"
"    }\"\n"
"  >\n"
"    Content\n"
"  </div>\n"
"</template>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
